      "source": [
        "## Results\n",
        "\n",
        "### Exploratory Data Analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "We conducted exploratory analyses on the four animal shelter datasets (Austin, Louisville, Sonoma, and Bloomington) to examine the relationships between our three key predictors: age at intake, breed type, and length of stay, and our key dependent variable of whether a dog was adopted."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### RQ1: Do younger dogs have higher adoption rates?\n",
        "\n",
        "To test whether age at intake predicts adoption, we computed each dog's age in months and binned it into five standard shelter-medicine categories: **Puppy** (0–6 months), **Juvenile** (6–18 months), **Young Adult** (1.5–3 years), **Adult** (3–7 years), and **Senior** (7+ years). Louisville was excluded from this analysis because the dataset does not contain an age variable, which leaves Austin, Sonoma, and Bloomington. We then calculated the adoption rate within each age group for every city and used chi-square tests of independence to determine whether the observed differences among age groups were statistically significant regarding adoption rates."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "image/png": "",
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "display_data"
        },
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "Pooled Chi-Square Test:  χ² = 2422.22,  df = 4,  p = 0.00e+00\n",
            "  → Significant (p < 0.05)\n",
            "\n",
            "Per-City Chi-Square Tests (consistency check):\n",
            "--------------------------------------------------\n",
            "  Austin:  χ² = 2531.02,  df = 4,  p = 0.00e+00  → Significant\n",
            "  Sonoma:  χ² = 1725.28,  df = 4,  p = 0.00e+00  → Significant\n",
            "  Bloomington:  χ² = 73.91,  df = 4,  p = 3.38e-15  → Significant\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import matplotlib.ticker as mtick\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "from scipy import stats\n",
        "import re\n",
        "\n",
        "# Using the four cleaned datasets loaded in the Data section above\n",
        "# (austin, sonoma, bloomington, louisville).\n",
        "# CSV columns load as strings — convert to datetime so we can subtract dates\n",
        "# (e.g., Intake Date minus Date Of Birth = age in Sonoma)\n",
        "for df, date_cols in [\n",
        "    (austin, [\"intake_datetime\", \"outcome_datetime\"]),\n",
        "    (sonoma, [\"Intake Date\", \"Outcome Date\", \"Date Of Birth\"]),\n",
        "    (bloomington, [\"intakedate\", \"movementdate\"]),\n",
        "    (louisville, [\"indate\", \"outdate\"]),\n",
        "]:\n",
        "    for col in date_cols:\n",
        "        if col in df.columns:\n",
        "            df[col] = pd.to_datetime(df[col], errors=\"coerce\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# defining the bins and labels for the age categories\n",
        "AGE_BINS   = [0, 6, 18, 36, 84, float(\"inf\")]\n",
        "AGE_LABELS = [\"Puppy\\n(0–6 mo)\", \"Juvenile\\n(6–18 mo)\", \"Young Adult\\n(1.5–3 yr)\",\n",
        "              \"Adult\\n(3–7 yr)\", \"Senior\\n(7+ yr)\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "# convert bloomington's open-response age to months\n",
        "def parse_bloomington_age(age_str):\n",
        "    if pd.isna(age_str) or str(age_str).strip() in (\"nan\", \"\"):\n",
        "        return np.nan\n",
        "    total = 0.0\n",
        "    for m in re.finditer(r\"(\\d+\\.?\\d*)\\s*(year|month|week|day)\", str(age_str).lower()):\n",
        "        val, unit = float(m.group(1)), m.group(2)\n",
        "        # map each unit to its equivalent in months\n",
        "        total += val * {\"year\": 12, \"month\": 1, \"week\": 1/4.345, \"day\": 1/30.44}[unit]\n",
        "    return total if total > 0 else np.nan\n",
        "\n",
        "# filter for dogs only\n",
        "def build_rq1_subset(df, city, age_col, outcome_col, adopt_label,\n",
        "                     species_col=None, species_val=None):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Filter a dataset to dogs only, extract age in months, classify adoption\n",
        "    as 1/0, and bin age into the shelter-medicine categories defined above.\"\"\"\n",
        "    sub = df.copy()\n",
        "    if species_col:\n",
        "        sub = sub[sub[species_col].str.strip().str.upper() == species_val.upper()]\n",
        "    age = pd.to_numeric(sub[age_col], errors=\"coerce\") # only selecting age column\n",
        "    adopted = (sub[outcome_col].str.strip().str.upper() == adopt_label.upper()).astype(int)\n",
        "    out = pd.DataFrame({\"city\": city, \"age_months\": age, \"adopted\": adopted}).dropna(subset=[\"age_months\"])\n",
        "    out = out[out[\"age_months\"] >= 0]\n",
        "    # making age bins into discrete age categories\n",
        "    out[\"age_category\"] = pd.cut(out[\"age_months\"], bins=AGE_BINS,\n",
        "                                  labels=AGE_LABELS, right=False, include_lowest=True)\n",
        "    return out\n",
        "\n",
        "# each dataset stores age differently so here we are coverting each dataset to be consistent for all\n",
        "#   Austin: age in days → divide by 30.44 to get months\n",
        "#   Sonoma: has Date Of Birth → subtract from Intake Date to get age in months\n",
        "#   Bloomington: free-text string → parse with regex function above\n",
        "rq1 = pd.concat([\n",
        "    build_rq1_subset(austin.assign(age_mo=austin[\"age_upon_intake_(days)\"] / 30.44),\n",
        "                     \"Austin\", \"age_mo\", \"outcome_type\", \"Adoption\", \"animal_type\", \"Dog\"),\n",
        "    build_rq1_subset(sonoma.assign(age_mo=(sonoma[\"Intake Date\"] - sonoma[\"Date Of Birth\"]).dt.total_seconds() / (3600*24*30.44)),\n",
        "                     \"Sonoma\", \"age_mo\", \"Outcome Type\", \"ADOPTION\", \"Type\", \"DOG\"),\n",
        "    build_rq1_subset(bloomington.assign(age_mo=bloomington[\"animalage\"].apply(parse_bloomington_age)),\n",
        "                     \"Bloomington\", \"age_mo\", \"movementtype\", \"Adoption\", \"speciesname\", \"Dog\"),\n",
        "], ignore_index=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "# --- Pooled bar chart: adoption rate by age category across all three cities combined ---\n",
        "CITY_ORDER = [\"Austin\", \"Sonoma\", \"Bloomington\"]\n",
        "AGE_LABELS_FLAT = [l.replace(\"\\n\", \" \") for l in AGE_LABELS]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Compute adoption rate and sample size for each age bin (all cities pooled)\n",
        "pooled = rq1.groupby(\"age_category\", observed=True)[\"adopted\"].agg([\"mean\", \"count\"]).reindex(AGE_LABELS)\n",
        "# Standard error of a binomial proportion for 95% CI error bars\n",
        "pooled[\"se\"] = np.sqrt(pooled[\"mean\"] * (1 - pooled[\"mean\"]) / pooled[\"count\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
        "x = np.arange(len(AGE_LABELS))\n",
        "\n",
        "bars = ax.bar(x, pooled[\"mean\"], yerr=pooled[\"se\"] * 1.96,\n",
        "              color=\"#3498db\", edgecolor=\"white\", capsize=5, alpha=0.85, width=0.6)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Label each bar with the adoption rate and sample size\n",
        "for i, (rate, n) in enumerate(zip(pooled[\"mean\"], pooled[\"count\"])):\n",
        "    ax.text(i, rate + pooled[\"se\"].iloc[i] * 1.96 + 0.02,\n",
        "            f\"{rate:.1%}\\n(n={int(n):,})\", ha=\"center\", va=\"bottom\", fontsize=9)\n",
        "\n",
        "ax.set_xticks(x)\n",
        "ax.set_xticklabels(AGE_LABELS_FLAT, fontsize=10)\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel(\"Age Category at Intake\", fontsize=11)\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel(\"Adoption Rate\", fontsize=11)\n",
        "ax.set_ylim(0, 0.80)\n",
        "ax.yaxis.set_major_formatter(mtick.PercentFormatter(xmax=1, decimals=0))\n",
        "ax.set_title(\"Adoption Rate by Age Category — Dogs Only\\n(Austin, Sonoma, and Bloomington combined)\",\n",
        "             fontsize=13, fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
        "sns.despine()\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.savefig(\"results/rq1_adoption_by_age.png\", dpi=150, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "# --- Chi-square test on the pooled data ---\n",
        "# H0: age category and adoption outcome are independent (no association)\n",
        "# A small p-value (< 0.05) means we reject H0 and conclude they are associated\n",
        "ct_pooled = pd.crosstab(rq1[\"age_category\"], rq1[\"adopted\"])\n",
        "chi2, p, dof, _ = stats.chi2_contingency(ct_pooled)\n",
        "print(f\"Pooled Chi-Square Test:  χ² = {chi2:.2f},  df = {dof},  p = {p:.2e}\")\n",
        "print(f\"  → {'Significant' if p < 0.05 else 'Not significant'} (p {'<' if p < 0.05 else '>='} 0.05)\")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Confirm the pattern holds within each city individually\n",
        "print(\"\\nIndependent chi-Square tests for each city (consistency check):\")\n",
        "print(\"-\" * 50)\n",
        "for city in CITY_ORDER:\n",
        "    ct = pd.crosstab(rq1[rq1[\"city\"]==city][\"age_category\"], rq1[rq1[\"city\"]==city][\"adopted\"])\n",
        "    chi2, p, dof, _ = stats.chi2_contingency(ct)\n",
        "    print(f\"  {city}:  χ² = {chi2:.2f},  df = {dof},  p = {p:.2e}  → {'Significant' if p < 0.05 else 'Not significant'}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "**RQ1 Findings:**\n",
        "\n",
        "When combining data across Austin, Sonoma, and Bloomington, adoption rates decline steadily with age. Puppies have the highest adoption rate, followed by juveniles and young adults, while seniors have the lowest. A chi-square test on the combined data confirms that this association between age category and adoption outcome is statistically significant (*p* < .001), supporting our first hypothesis that younger dogs are more likely to be adopted.\n",
        "\n",
        "This pattern is representative of only a single city, but rather three cities. Chi-square tests of each city show the relationship between age and adoption rates is independently significant in Austin, Sonoma, and Bloomington (all *p* < .001), which strengthens our confidence that the finding generalizes across shelters with different capacities and regions.\n",
        "\n",
        "One limitation is that the data quality of age varies across datasets. Austin records age in days (which is highly precise), Sonoma computes it from a date-of-birth field that may be estimated for strays, and Bloomington uses open-response entries (e.g.,\"2 years\"), which introduces some guessing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### RQ2: Do purebred dogs have higher adoption rates than mixed-breed dogs?\n",
        "\n",
        "To test whether giving dogs labels for possible breed classification influences adoption, we classified each dog as **Purebred** or **Mixed** based on whether its breed field contained indicators such as \"Mix,\" \"/\", or \"Cross.\" In other words, we've collapsed the breed types into binary bins so that we avoid comparing hundreds of inconsistent breed labels. Furthermore, this binary approach allows us to investigate the stigma between purebred preference and mixed-breed. All four cities are included in this analysis. We computed adoption rates by breed type per city and tested for statistical association using chi-square tests."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [
        {
          "data": {
            "image/png": "",
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1000x500 with 1 Axes>"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "output_type": "display_data"
        },
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "\n",
            "Chi-Square Tests: Breed Type vs. Adoption Outcome\n",
            "============================================================\n",
            "\n",
            "Austin:  χ² = 222.32,  df = 1,  p = 2.82e-50\n",
            "  → Significant (p < 0.05)\n",
            "\n",
            "Louisville:  χ² = 111.23,  df = 1,  p = 5.27e-26\n",
            "  → Significant (p < 0.05)\n",
            "\n",
            "Sonoma:  χ² = 272.62,  df = 1,  p = 3.05e-61\n",
            "  → Significant (p < 0.05)\n",
            "\n",
            "Bloomington:  χ² = 37.91,  df = 1,  p = 7.40e-10\n",
            "  → Significant (p < 0.05)\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# classify breed as Mixed or Purebred using keyword heuristics.\n",
        "# in other words, if the breed string contains \"Mix\", \"/\", or \"Cross\" it is labeled Mixed.\n",
        "def classify_breed(breed_str):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Classify a breed string as 'Mixed' or 'Purebred'.\"\"\"\n",
        "    if pd.isna(breed_str):\n",
        "        return \"Unknown\"\n",
        "    b = breed_str.upper()\n",
        "    return \"Mixed\" if (\"MIX\" in b or \"/\" in b or \"CROSS\" in b) else \"Purebred\"\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_rq2_subset(df, city, breed_col, outcome_col, adopt_label,\n",
        "                     species_col=None, species_val=None):\n",
        "    \"\"\"Filter to dogs, apply the breed classifier, and create a binary adopted column.\"\"\"\n",
        "    sub = df.copy()\n",
        "    if species_col:\n",
        "        sub = sub[sub[species_col] == species_val]\n",
        "    return pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "        \"city\": city,\n",
        "        \"breed_type\": sub[breed_col].apply(classify_breed),\n",
        "        \"adopted\": (sub[outcome_col] == adopt_label).astype(int)\n",
        "    })\n",
        "\n",
        "# combine into one dataframe\n",
        "rq2 = pd.concat([\n",
        "    build_rq2_subset(austin, \"Austin\", \"breed\", \"outcome_type\", \"Adoption\", \"animal_type\", \"Dog\"),\n",
        "    build_rq2_subset(louisville, \"Louisville\", \"breed\", \"outtype\", \"ADOPTION\", \"animaltype\", \"DOG\"),\n",
        "    build_rq2_subset(sonoma, \"Sonoma\", \"Breed\", \"Outcome Type\", \"ADOPTION\", \"Type\", \"DOG\"),\n",
        "    build_rq2_subset(bloomington, \"Bloomington\", \"breedname\", \"movementtype\", \"Adoption\", \"speciesname\", \"Dog\"),\n",
        "], ignore_index=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "# drop rows where breed could not be determined\n",
        "rq2 = rq2[rq2[\"breed_type\"] != \"Unknown\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "# visualization for RQ2\n",
        "CITY_ORDER_4 = [\"Austin\", \"Louisville\", \"Sonoma\", \"Bloomington\"]\n",
        "BREED_COLORS = {\"Mixed\": \"#5B9BD5\", \"Purebred\": \"#ED7D31\"}\n",
        "\n",
